 ## Background
-The Adaptive Gaussian Selector is part of the FlexGS method, introduced in "FlexGS: Train Once, Deploy Everywhere with Many-in-One Flexible 3D Gaussian Splatting" [S1]. It addresses the limitation of fixed heuristic selection rules which may fail to generalize in extreme cases (e.g., selecting 1% of Gaussians) and the need for importance scores to be frequently re-computed as Gaussian attributes evolve during training [S1]. The method builds on 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) [18] and utilizes Gumbel-Softmax [16] for differentiable sampling.
+The Adaptive Gaussian Selector is part of the FlexGS method, introduced in "FlexGS: Train Once, Deploy Everywhere with Many-in-One Flexible 3D Gaussian Splatting" [S1]. It addresses the limitation of fixed heuristic selection rules which may fail to generalize in extreme cases (e.g., selecting 1% of Gaussians) and the need for importance scores to be frequently re-computed as Gaussian attributes evolve during training [S1]. The method builds on 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) [18] and utilizes Gumbel-Softmax [16] for differentiable sampling [S1].
 
